$162$ and $178$ are each $1$ standard deviation from $170$.
$P(162 < X < 178)$
$= 0.68$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.2cm, y=1cm]
\fill[gray!35] (-1,0) -- plot[domain=-1:1, samples=40, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (1,0) -- cycle;
\draw[thick] plot[domain=-3.7:3.7, samples=80, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[->] (-4.1,0) -- (4.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw (-1,0) -- (-1,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$162$};
\draw (0,0) -- (0,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$170$};
\draw (1,0) -- (1,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$178$};
\node at (0,1.1) {$0.68$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$1.95$ kg is $1$ standard deviation above $1.8$ kg.
$P(X > 1.95)$
$= (1 - 0.68) \div 2$
$= 0.16$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.2cm, y=1cm]
\fill[gray!35] (1,0) -- plot[domain=1:3.7, samples=50, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (3.7,0) -- cycle;
\draw[thick] plot[domain=-3.7:3.7, samples=80, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[->] (-4.1,0) -- (4.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw (0,0) -- (0,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$1.8$};
\draw (1,0) -- (1,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$1.95$};
\node at (2.3,1.3) {$0.16$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$55$ minutes is $3$ standard deviations above $46$ minutes.
$P(X < 55)$
$= 0.5 + 0.4985$
$= 0.9985$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.2cm, y=1cm]
\fill[gray!35] (-3.7,0) -- plot[domain=-3.7:3, samples=70, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (3,0) -- cycle;
\draw[thick] plot[domain=-3.7:3.7, samples=80, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[->] (-4.1,0) -- (4.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw (0,0) -- (0,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$46$};
\draw (3,0) -- (3,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$55$};
\node at (0,1.1) {$0.9985$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$48$ and $52$ are $2$ standard deviations from $50$, and $49$ and $51$ are $1$ standard deviation from $50$.
$P(48 < X < 49) + P(51 < X < 52)$
$= 0.135 + 0.135$
$= 0.27$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.2cm, y=1cm]
\fill[gray!35] (-2,0) -- plot[domain=-2:-1, samples=40, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (-1,0) -- cycle;
\fill[gray!35] (1,0) -- plot[domain=1:2, samples=40, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (2,0) -- cycle;
\draw[thick] plot[domain=-3.7:3.7, samples=80, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[->] (-4.1,0) -- (4.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw (-2,0) -- (-2,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$48$};
\draw (-1,0) -- (-1,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$49$};
\draw (1,0) -- (1,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$51$};
\draw (2,0) -- (2,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$52$};
\node at (-1.5,1.9) {$0.135$};
\node at (1.5,1.9) {$0.135$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$25$ is $3$ standard deviations below $55$ and $65$ is $1$ standard deviation above.
$P(25 < X < 65)$
$= 0.4985 + 0.34$
$= 0.8385$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.2cm, y=1cm]
