\draw[->] (-4.1,0) -- (4.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw (-3,0) -- (-3,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$25$};
\draw (0,0) -- (0,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$55$};
\draw (1,0) -- (1,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$65$};
\node at (-0.7,1.1) {$0.8385$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$46$ is $1$ standard deviation above $40$.
$P(X > 46) = (1 - 0.68) \div 2 = 0.16$
$f = np$
$= 900 \times 0.16$
$= 144$ plants
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.2cm, y=1cm]
\fill[gray!35] (1,0) -- plot[domain=1:3.7, samples=50, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (3.7,0) -- cycle;
\draw[thick] plot[domain=-3.7:3.7, samples=80, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[->] (-4.1,0) -- (4.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw (0,0) -- (0,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$40$};
\draw (1,0) -- (1,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$46$};
\node at (2.3,1.3) {$0.16$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$1100$ L is $2$ standard deviations below $1500$ L.
$P(1100 < X < 1500) = 0.95 \div 2 = 0.475$
$f = np$
$= 2400 \times 0.475$
$= 1140$ households
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.2cm, y=1cm]
\fill[gray!35] (-2,0) -- plot[domain=-2:0, samples=40, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (0,0) -- cycle;
\draw[thick] plot[domain=-3.7:3.7, samples=80, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[->] (-4.1,0) -- (4.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw (-2,0) -- (-2,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$1100$};
\draw (0,0) -- (0,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$1500$};
\node at (-1,0.9) {$0.475$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$90 = 72 + 3(6)$, so the time is $3$ standard deviations above the mean.
$P(X > 90)$
$= (1 - 0.997) \div 2$
$= 0.0015$
Only about $0.15\%$ of assembly times are this long, so $90$ seconds is unusual.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.2cm, y=1cm]
\fill[gray!35] (3,0) -- plot[domain=3:3.7, samples=40, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (3.7,0) -- cycle;
\draw[thick] plot[domain=-3.7:3.7, samples=80, smooth, variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[->] (-4.1,0) -- (4.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw (0,0) -- (0,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$72$};
\draw (3,0) -- (3,-0.12) node[below, font=\small] {$90$};
\node at (3.4,1.1) {$0.0015$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
